xcursor: preserve constness for C23 strchr

C23 makes the string functions preserve const qualification, so strchr() on a
const input can return a const-qualified pointer.  xcursor_next_path() only uses
the result as a read-only cursor, so keep the const qualifier to avoid
-Wdiscarded-qualifiers when wlroots builds with -Werror.

Signed-off-by: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>

--- a/xcursor/xcursor.c
+++ b/xcursor/xcursor.c
@@ -602,7 +602,7 @@ xcursor_build_fullname(const char *dir, const char *subdir, const char *file)
 static const char *
 xcursor_next_path(const char *path)
 {
-	char *colon = strchr(path, ':');
+	const char *colon = strchr(path, ':');
 
 	if (!colon)
 		return NULL;
